   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the village of Endicott to offer an optional twenty year\nretirement plan to a certain police officer employed by such village",
    "basePrintNo": "S2093",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2093-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2093\n\nSPONSOR: AKSHAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the village of Endicott to offer an optional twenty\nyear retirement plan to a certain police officer employed by such\nvillage\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the legislation is to allow the village of Endicott to\nreopen the provisions of Section 384-d of the Retirement and Social\n\nSecurity Law for police officer Jennifer Quinn.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Allows the Village of Endicott to offer an optional twenty\nyear retirement plan contained in section 384-d to police officer Jenni-\nfer Quinn, rather than the section 375-I plan which she was incorrectly\nenrolled.\n\nSection 2: Allows the Village of Endicott to amortize the cost over a\nfive year period.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJennifer Quinn was employed with the Village of Endicott Police Depart-\nment as an officer beginning on August 7, 2000. Through no fault of her\nown, she failed to file a timely application in the special twenty year\nretirement plan contained in section 384-d of the retirement and social\nsecurity law which resulted in her being places in the section 375-i,\nthe incorrect plan. All other members of the Village's Police Department\nare in Section 384-d of the Retirement System.\n\nThe Village of Endicott and Jennifer Quinn have requested that she be\nallowed to be placed in the section 375-I plan. The Village Board passed\na resolution on May 9, 2017 requesting that the Village be granted the\napproval to move Ms. Quinn to her preferred plan. The village of Endi-\ncott will be responsible for paying the past cost services to the\nretirement system.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.8281 - Died in Civil Service and Pensions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications to the State; all past\nservice costs associated with implementing the provisions of this act\nshall be borne by the Village of Endicott and may be amortized over a\nperiod of five years. The total cost of past service is $127,000.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
